      "content": "that's much more intense, i like the direction it's going. \n\nyou mentioned that not voting is \"implicitly barring progressive forces.\" can you actually expand on that part of the speech? i want a specific paragraph that argues why voting 'lesser of two evils' is actually a moral necessity to protect progress, and how failing to do so isn't just a personal choice, but a way of actively facilitating the rise of reactionary or regressive movements. basically, make the argument that if you aren't actively voting to protect progress, you are effectively voting for its destruction.",
